cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "admissible: auditing whether exome data can support an interpretation"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shahbazi
    given-names: Amir
repository-code: "https://github.com/shahbazigenomics/admissible"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-12"
keywords:
  - exome sequencing
  - sample identity
  - quality control
  - rare disease
  - pedigree
abstract: >-
  A command-line tool that audits the evidence base for a genomic interpretation
  rather than the interpretation itself: sample identity and pedigree
  consistency, genotype confidence, call-set provenance, callable fraction, and
  the inheritance-model count profile. It reads only the user's own files and
  bundles no annotation database.
